{
    "background_story": "Rocky was a mango who had been left on the tree for too long. Once a vibrant yellow, he had ripened to a deep orange and was now on the verge of being overripe. Despite his slightly soft skin, Rocky was determined to make the most of his situation. He realized that his sweetness and juiciness could still be enjoyed, even if he wasn't as firm as he used to be. Rocky became the star of the fruit salad, adding a burst of flavor and aroma that no other fruit could match. As he was savored by those who ate him, Rocky felt proud to have found a way to make his overripe state a virtue, rather than a liability. His story spread among the fruit community, inspiring others to find the silver lining in their own imperfections.",
